   Library doc gaps found on the way are in SC-253 (owner-gated). *@

<PageTitle>Column reorder — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Column reorder" Category="Data Grid" CategoryHref="demo/grid" ControlName="GridControl"
                   Tagline="Drag a header sideways and drop it where the column should go."
                   SourcePath="Grid/GridControl.razor;Grid/GridControl.razor.cs;Grid/GridSettings.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>AllowColumnReorder</code> is on by default: every header is draggable, and while a header is being dragged the grid shows a
            vertical pipe at the position where the column would land. Drop to the left half of a header to land before it, to the right
            half to land after it. <code>ColumnReorderPipeColor</code> takes any CSS colour for the pipe; the default is a dark grey. After a drop the grid raises
            <code>OnLayoutChanged</code> with a <code>GridSettings</code> snapshot whose <code>ColumnOrder</code> lists the fields in their new
            order, which is what a host saves to restore a user's layout later.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="reorder" Title="Move columns by dragging headers" RazorCode="@Code.Reorder" CSharpCode="@Code.ReorderCs">
            <Description><p>Drag <strong>Priority</strong> in front of <strong>Model</strong>, or <strong>Owner</strong> to the right of <strong>Cost</strong>. Only the dragged column moves; sorting, filtering and the search box keep working on the new order.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <GridControl TValue="ReorderingRow"
                             DataSource="@_rows"
                             AllowSelection="true"
                             AllowSorting="true"
                             AllowFiltering="true"
                             AllowGrouping="false"
                             AllowResizing="true"
                             AllowColumnReorder="true"
                             EnableHover="true"
                             ShowSearchBar="true"
                             Height="520px"
                             OnLayoutChanged="LayoutChanged">
                    <GridColumnsBase>
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Model)"       HeaderText="Model"        Width="130px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Community)"   HeaderText="Community"    Width="150px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Phase)"       HeaderText="Phase"        Width="120px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Task)"        HeaderText="Task"         Width="220px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Owner)"       HeaderText="Owner"        Width="150px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Priority)"    HeaderText="Priority"     Width="100px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Hours)"       HeaderText="Hours"        Width="90px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="N1" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.Cost)"        HeaderText="Cost"         Width="120px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C2" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ReorderingRow.LastUpdated)" HeaderText="Last Updated" Width="130px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Date" Format="d" />
                    </GridColumnsBase>
                </GridControl>
                <p class="result">@(_order is null ? "Drop a header to see the new order here." : $"Order: {_order}")</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="GridControl parameters for reordering and layout" Rows="Vocab.Grid" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="GridSettings" Rows="Vocab.Settings" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="IGridSettingsStore" Rows="Vocab.Store" />
        <p>
            The host registers one <code>IGridSettingsStore</code>, scoped or singleton; with none registered the grid does not persist. There is no
            public method that returns or applies a <code>GridSettings</code> on its own; <code>GetState()</code> and <code>SetStateAsync()</code>
            round-trip the wider <code>GridState</code>, which includes the column layout, and <code>EndUpdateAsync</code> or
            <code>SuspendRedraw</code> take a final column order (see <a href="demo/grid/column-swap">Column sets</a>). Besides dragging, the
            header menu's Choose Columns dialog moves a column with its Move Up and Move Down buttons. There is no per-column switch, so a host
            that must keep one column in place has to turn <code>AllowColumnReorder</code> off.
        </p>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="demo/grid">Grid overview</a>: the core flags on a small list.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/grid/column-swap">Column sets</a>: the host swaps whole column sets instead of the user dragging.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/grid/advanced">Frozen columns</a>: columns pinned to an edge.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

